FILE: app/src/jump-to-frame.ts
```ts
import { goToFrame, playAnimation } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { AnimationGroup } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function jumpToFrame(group: AnimationGroup, frame: number): void {
    goToFrame(group, frame);
    playAnimation(group);
}
```

I created `src/jump-to-frame.ts` with a two-line implementation: `goToFrame` sets the group's time (converting frame to seconds via its frameRate) and pauses it, then `playAnimation` resumes it from that point, preserving speed, loop mode, and weight. I'm not sure of anything — the notes confirm `goToFrame` pauses and `playAnimation` resumes for both glTF and property groups, so the pair covers both clip kinds and both loop settings.
